on't think this is my favorite  Catwoman I do this is definitely not my  favorite Riddler but they are exactly  the right versions of each of these  characters for this movie this setting  this tone in this story  they don't have to be the best in the  bat in a vacuum because they were the  right ones for this iteration  it's just something that I mean saying  something is more than the sum of his  Parts is a bit of a cliche but it really  is it really is it takes component parts  that individually I didn't have a lot of  interest in  but it's using them because they fit so  well together  it is a three-hour movie that does not  feel like it's that long it is so well  focused it it truly brought in the Noir  and the detective sense which was  something that they had said they were  going to do but I didn't believe them  but they they actually did it  and I'm genuinely excited for more of  this iteration of Batman and I have not  been able to say that about any  adaptation of Batman in a while  number seven  the Sandman now this one is placement is  a little bit weird it's certainly not  better than the original and I do deeply  love the original  and part of my love of this is as an  adaptation when I did a video on this it  wasn't straight up a review it was to  talk about how intelligently adapted it  was because knowing the original as well  as I know it and seeing what they took  on board what they tweaked and noticing  okay  for the reason I think that they did  that that's a really smart change  the adaptations were so smart and it  preserved pretty much everything that  you would want preserved about Sandman  while tweaking things that weren't  necessarily flaws in the original but  now work better for the way it's being  presented that was a smart change and  those are across the board all over the  place it it is just good flat out but I  experienced it as an adaptation and it  is a masterful adaptation  number six  Glass Onion  just barely squeaked in towa